            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bypass and fan-powered units use little electricity, plus some water to the drain, so a season usually costs tens of dollars plus a water panel. Steam units boil their water, so a unit averaging four gallons a day can use about $280 of electricity over a 150-day season at 17 cents per kWh."
          }
        },
