          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A humidifier costs $30 to $150 to buy for one room and $400 to $2,500 installed for the whole house, but the type you choose decides most of what you will spend after that. Ultrasonic and evaporative units are cheap to run; warm mist and steam units pay for boiling every gallon; and bottled distilled water can quietly become the largest bill of all.
          </p>
